            {
              "type": "added",
              "content": "The sandbox depends on platform support and, on Linux, tools like `bubblewrap` and `socat`. When `enabled` is `true` and the sandbox can't start, `query()` reports a `result` message with `subtype: \"error_during_execution\"` and the reason in `errors`. For a single message `query()` call, the SDK throws after yielding that error result, so wrap the loop in a try block to continue past it. See [Handle the result](/en/agent-sdk/agent-loop#handle-the-result) for the error contract."
            },
            {
              "type": "context",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "context",
              "content": "To run unsandboxed instead, set `failIfUnavailable: false`."
